.TH CUBE-EDITOR 1 "October 2026" "Cube Editor 0.5.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cube-editor-studio, cube-editor-cli \- customize and rebuild Linux live images
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cube-editor-studio
.RI [ project ]
.RI [ --page " page" ]
.br
.B cube-editor-cli
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Cube Editor Studio is a GTK 4 desktop workspace for persistent Ubuntu and
Debian live ISO projects, package recipes, payload files, restore points,
recovery, image exports and virtual machine tests.
.PP
The standalone package installs alongside Whitecube's bundled editor without
replacing its launcher. Use cube-editor-studio for the standalone application.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --version
Print the installed version without opening a display.
.TP
.B --help
Show the available options or CLI commands.
.TP
.B --cli
Pass subsequent arguments to the CLI when using cube-editor-studio.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
cube-editor-studio /path/to/project
cube-editor-cli dependencies
cube-editor-cli inspect /path/to/source.iso
cube-editor-cli plan /path/to/project build
.fi
.SH PRIVILEGES
The interface runs as your normal user. Filesystem operations authenticate with
sudo inside a terminal. Guest executables and recipes run with host root
privileges; use only trusted inputs. The chroot is not a security sandbox.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/cube-editor/recent.json
Recent projects.
.TP
.I ~/cubic/work
Default project directory.
.TP
.I ~/cubic/complete
Default output directory.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/cube-editor/README.md.gz
Full workflow and recovery documentation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xorriso (1),
.BR mksquashfs (1),
.BR qemu-system-x86_64 (1)
